139:{character:player}That's right, but they might not understand what "idling" means.
140:{character:Nadeshiko}Oh, that's a good point. I'll explain that then. Hmm... Simply put, idling is the lowest stable rotational speed of an engine when there is no load.
141:{character:player}Maybe you'll also need to explain what "no load" means.
142:{character:Nadeshiko}!?
143:{character:player}Trust me.
144:{character:Nadeshiko}Fine. I've been exposed to this since I was little, so it is sometimes difficult for me to judge how much of this is general knowledge.
145:{character:player}That's okay. Let me play the role of the general public.
146:{character:Nadeshiko}Haha, thanks!
148:Daylight floods the classroom, moving slowly across the room.
149:With my feedback and our discussion, Nadeshiko quickly adapts to a new teaching rhythm. She talks less and less as she begins to revise her teaching plan quickly.
150:*Ringing* Nadeshiko's alarm tells us that the one-hour lecture has already ended.
151:Nadeshiko is fully focused on revising her PPT and doesn't hear the alarm at all.
152:Looking at how seriously she is working, I decide to wait for her to finish.
153:{character:player}Have you finished revising the teaching plan?
154:{character:Nadeshiko}Yeah, I was thinking of making some simple revision marks during class time, but I got too engaged by mistake. Did you deliberately not remind me when the alarm rang?
155:{character:player}I can't help it. Nadeshiko, you looked so focused I couldn't bear to disturb you.
157:{character:player}Anyway, instead of fixating on this, why don't we make the most of our time. Did you say there's also a practical assessment? I'm really looking forward to that!
158:{character:Nadeshiko}...Hmm, that's right. There's a practical assessment next. The indoor training is pointless since you already know how to ride a motorcycle. Why don't I take you to a great outdoor training ground?
159:I get to take this opportunity to go outdoors. Why not?
160:After eating a simple work meal, we happily go to the outdoor motorcycle venue Nadeshiko had reserved.
163:The person riding it is Nadeshiko, the female biker who invited me today.
164:{character:Nadeshiko}I'll put on a show for you to thank you for waiting so long for me.
165:{character:player}Awesome!
167:Nadeshiko suggested this to me ten minutes ago, and I naturally said yes.
168:Nadeshiko demonstrates a series of technically difficult moves smoothly, drifting up to me and stopping with a flick of the tail. She takes off her helmet, brushes her long hair behind her head, and quickly locks her eyes on me.
169:{character:player}...Oh!
170:I start clapping a few seconds late after hearing the bursts of applause from the other motorcycle enthusiasts next to the track.
171:{character:Nadeshiko}Haha... Judging from your reaction, you must be tired from all the mental work you've done in the morning.
172:{character:player}To be honest, I'm absolutely stunned. This is my first time seeing a motorcycle performance from such a close distance. It's so... beautiful.
173:At a loss for words, I can only use such a plain word to express my admiration.
174:{character:player}No matter how much I practice, I don't think I'll ever achieve such a combination of strength and beauty like yours.
175:Nadeshiko starts laughing.
176:{character:Nadeshiko}I bend over while driving to reduce the wind resistance. Bending appropriately when accelerating into corners increases friction, which helps to maintain control over the motorcycle when moving forward into a curve. The standard riding position is to keep the muscles relaxed and maintain stamina during long rides. In short, the poses you see are not intended to just look beautiful.
177:{character:Nadeshiko}They're mainly done to maintain control. The reason you think they look beautiful is that I can control the motorcycle very well in these positions. The aura you have when you're in complete control will naturally shock people. I've just done this with a motorcycle.
178:{character:player}Ah, so according to what you're saying, achieving control can enhance one's charisma no matter what field they are in...
179:{character:Nadeshiko}Yes, just like how lots of people can't take their eyes off you when you're in control and in your element while playing mahjong.
180:{character:player}Eh? For real?
181:{character:Nadeshiko}Have some confidence. I don't give praise easily.
182:{character:player}Haha, thanks. But this is your home field today. Since today's goal is to test out a motorcycle driving course for beginners, let's stick to the basics and start from the very beginning.
183:{character:Nadeshiko}Sure, please share more of your opinions with me.
184:{character:player}No problem!
185:The training has officially started. Compared with the theory class, Nadeshiko appears more confident while teaching me how to drive a motorcycle.
186:She follows the driving training process and tells me all the steps in order, clearly and concisely. By the end of the teaching demonstration process, I managed to complete the goal of the test: drive a motorcycle in a straight line at a speed comparable to that of a bicycle.
187:Nadeshiko claps at me.
188:{character:Nadeshiko}That was beautifully done. I'm impressed!
189:{character:player}I thought you don't give praises so easily?!
190:{character:Nadeshiko}Haha, forget about the details. Come on, let's finish the rest of the process.
191:The experience of the practical training is pretty good. All she needs to do is make some minor adjustments to her communication methods and the terms she uses when talking to students. I'm very confident that Nadeshiko will pass her interview tomorrow.
192:After another round of discussion and feedback, we end the practical training with a happy atmosphere.
193:By the time we return to the city after leaving the venue, the sky has already become dark.
194:{character:Nadeshiko}Time sure passes quickly. It's already so late. Do you want to have a drink with me?
195:{character:player}It's her interview tomorrow... Should I go with her?
197:{character:Nadeshiko}Thanks for being so thoughtful and considerate. Come with me. The training ground of this driving school is ready.
198:Driving Instructor
199:{character:Driving Instructor}Hahaha! So you're the student Nadeshiko invited over to practice on? Welcome! Just act like you're at home while you're here at our training ground! Use whichever motorcycle you fancy!
200:{character:player}Ahahaha, thanks...
201:I respond awkwardly but politely to the old driving school instructor who shakes my hand enthusiastically. I look quizzically at Nadeshiko next to me for an answer.
202:{character:Nadeshiko}This is one of my motorcycle instructors. Well, actually, my father is a mechanic at this driving school, and the instructors here have known us for years. I only have a chance to get this part-time job this time because of these guys.
203:{character:player}I see.
204:{character:Driving Instructor}Hahaha, Nadeshiko, you're being too humble. Based on what we know about her, Nadeshiko should have no problem getting that part-time instructor position, but she has always been this way. Once she decides on something, she must do her best meticulously.
205:{character:Nadeshiko}Hey, old man! How many times have I told you not to treat me like a little girl now...
206:{character:Driving Instructor}Hahaha, don't expect me to change now since I watched you grow up. Speaking of which, time has passed so quickly. In the blink of an eye, that little girl who was only as tall as a tire has become an adult... and a motorcycle enthusiast at that! I would never imagine that happening when you were in high school.
207:{character:Driving Instructor}Oh yeah! I still have a group photo of you from when you were in high school. Let me look for it...
208:{character:Nadeshiko}?!
209:The driving instructor reaches for his mobile phone to search for the photo, but Nadeshiko steps forward and stops him instantly.
210:{character:Nadeshiko}No, that won't be necessary. Just go, old man. We need to use our time wisely.
211:{character:Driving Instructor}Oh... I guess you're right. Let's chat again next time then. I'll leave this place to you guys.
212:For some reason, I feel like I saw a trace of embarrassment on Nadeshiko's face, but it might just be my imagination.
213:We finally start the practical training after that brief episode.
214:Compared with the theory class, Nadeshiko appears more confident while teaching me how to drive a motorcycle.
215:She follows the driving training process and tells me all the steps in order, clearly and concisely. After she demonstrates everything to me once, my eyes and brain tell me I've learned how to do it.
216:{character:Nadeshiko}Now, {var:player_nickname}, please start your first driving practice.
217:Hearing her say that makes me, who was full of confidence earlier, suddenly feel nervous.
218:{character:Nadeshiko}I'm right here.
