220:{character:Nadeshiko}That was beautifully executed! You're very talented!
221:{character:player}Isn't it a bit over the top to praise me so much for a basic technique?
222:{character:Nadeshiko}Encouragement is important to beginners. After all, the most important thing to driving a motorcycle is confidence!
224:{character:Nadeshiko}That's right, but you'll need to overcome this mentality to become an outstanding biker. Once you overcome these things, you'll be able to control the motorcycle like it's an extension of your body and experience the unique freedom and exhilarating journey of a motorcycle through it.
225:Nadeshiko's eyes shine brightly and passionately when she talks about this.
226:{character:player}Nadeshiko, do you have any special experience in this regard?
227:{character:Nadeshiko}Well... You need to constantly practice and gain experience to achieve this. In fact, you undertake a certain amount of risk just by choosing to enjoy riding a motorcycle because all kinds of emergencies are possible. I remember when hail fell suddenly one time while I was driving on a winding mountain road, which made the mountain road wet and slippery. I accidentally slipped into a ravine with my motorcycle.
228:{character:player}Geez! What happened after that?
229:{character:Nadeshiko}Fortunately, a road camera confirmed the cause of the accident, and the insurance company paid for the damaged chassis, dashboard, engine, and tires.
230:{character:player}Hold on, I'm asking about you, not the motorcycle!
231:{character:Nadeshiko}Me? Hmm, I guess I did get hurt, but where was it again?
232:She can say which parts of the motorcycle were damaged without thinking, but she has no memory of the injuries she suffered?
233:{character:Nadeshiko}Ahaha, you look so surprised. You think it's unbelievable, right?
234:{character:Nadeshiko}How should I say this... I was mentally prepared to get injured the moment I chose to become a biker, so I won't purposefully remember my injuries. However, when it comes to my motorcycle, I think of it as an important partner who I care for like a relative or friend rather than just a vehicle. My heart hurts every time it gets hurt.
236:{character:Nadeshiko}Of course, the hefty repair bill is another reason why I remember this so well.
237:...Now she's being practical all of a sudden!
238:{character:Nadeshiko}Anyway, I know these complicated feelings aren't the easiest things to understand.
239:{character:player}...Well, although I haven't started to think of a motorcycle as my companion yet, I do feel like riding a motorcycle outdoors is a way to relax. After all, there aren't many ways to enjoy freedom, relaxation, and the scenery all at the same time in our everyday lives.
240:Nadeshiko turns to look at me suddenly while I'm saying this. Her bright and passionate eyes focus on me.
241:{character:Nadeshiko}{var:player_nickname}, the fact that you think this already makes me look at you in a different light. Come on, let's finish the lesson and then have a good chat.
242:{character:player}Sure!
243:{character:player}Okay, is there any place you recommend?
244:{character:Nadeshiko}Of course.
245:{character:Nadeshiko}Ahhh! There's nothing better than a glass of cold beer to relieve fatigue at this time!
246:{character:player}You've had a long day today. Good luck with the interview tomorrow!
247:{character:Nadeshiko}You're the one who has been working hard today. Good thing you were around to help me today. But...
