503:Reject the invitation because you don't want to ruin her interview tomorrow
505:Half an hour later
506:Izakaya
507:After sending my reply to Nadeshiko, I open the Watafak Moment video pushed to me on the CatChat homepage. As I eat breakfast leisurely, I watch other people's Blessing of Heaven and Thirteen Orphans enviously.
508:Although the Watafak Moment is very interesting, my hands always get itchy to play mahjong if I watch it for too long. I look at the bright sun outside the window and decide to go play mahjong at a dojo and have a good time on the weekend with my skills.
509:I take out my phone quickly and log in to CatChat. Sure enough, there's an unread message from Nadeshiko. It's her reply to my message, and it says: "You're the lucky winner. I'll come to pick you up, so don't go anywhere."
510:Nadeshiko often posts photos of her riding a motorcycle on CatChat. I once thought it would be very nice to have a chance to ride a motorcycle with her. Is today the day my dream comes true?
511:One hour later
512:The howling sound of the engine surrounds my ears like the roaring of a beast. At this moment, a dark metal beast is roaring and galloping on this track.
513:I lie on the bed, waving my sore arms and legs. I look at my phone with sleepy eyes and start a mahjong game to play a round before I sleep.
514:Suddenly, I receive a video call from Nadeshiko.
515:After a day of lessons, I return home and lie on the bed after tidying up. My accumulated fatigue suddenly surfaces all at once.
516:{character:player}I think that it's great to be so focused. For example, when you ride your motorcycle, your keen awareness and control of direction and road conditions are made possible by your high degree of concentration. I'm also like that when I play mahjong and think about how to take control of the game. It's quite common for me to lose track of the time and everything happening around me.
517:{character:Nadeshiko}But? But what? What's there to hesitate about?
518:{character:Nadeshiko}Oh, I understand. If you don't want to ride your own motorcycle, my back seat is always available for you. How about that? Are you interested now?
519:In the training ground of the driving school
520:Accept the invitation without thinking too much about it
521:Decline the invitation because you don't want to ruin her interview tomorrow
522:{character:Nadeshiko}Because my decision was rather last minute, Chihori suggested that I use a lottery to select people. She said that I'll get more replies and be able to reach my target audience more precisely.
523:{character:Nadeshiko}Are you surprised? Because my decision was rather last minute, Chihori suggested that I use a lottery to select people. She said that I'll get more replies and be able to reach my target audience more precisely.
524:Time passes quickly while Nadeshiko and I discuss how she should revise her teaching plan.
525:A complete motorcycle beginner, here to lower the chance of winning the prize for everyone else.
526:Already has a license, feeling sad about losing the opportunity. Still curious about the prize tho.
528:Narration
531:This is a professional outdoor motorcycle training ground. On both sides of the track are beautifully maintained strips of grass. The green scenery is refreshing and prevents passing motorcycles from entering by mistake.
532:After typing the last word, Nadeshiko finally breaks out of her state of concentration. She breathes a sigh of relief and looks surprised after she turns to look at me.
533:{character:player}Although I really want to go to the outdoor training ground, I should start with the standard indoor training ground since I'm a novice. This would also be the more likely scenario when you have real students.
534:{character:player}That makes sense. Just now, I saw you use all these techniques so easily, but I still feel nervous when I try to do them myself, especially when I feel the resistance of the wind blowing in my face after speeding up.
535:Yeah, it's something she cherishes, after all. When I think about my collector's edition mahjong set and how I would feel if any of the tiles has a crack, I feel like I can really relate to her sentiment.
